<section class="sec" id="roles" style="padding-top:60px"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="route-wrap">
    <svg class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><line class="base" x1="30" x2="30" y1="0" y2="100%"/><line class="ink rail-ink" x1="30" x2="30" y1="0" y2="0"/></svg>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2026 – now</span><small>ApexPaths<br>Lahore</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Founder, ApexPaths</h3>
        <div class="role">Founder of ApexPaths · Co-founder of FINSTRIDE</div>
        <div class="body"><p>ApexPaths is a small, independent app studio. Its first app, FINSTRIDE, is a personal finance app for the web and phone, co-founded with Bismah Khalid.</p><p>I took FINSTRIDE from an Excel model to a working product: the data model, the logic, security with two-step login, passkeys and rate limiting, offline entry, receipt scanning and payments in testing. The open beta starts on 16 November 2026. The second app, ACTUVISTA, is about halfway built.</p></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2026 – now</span><small>Freelance<br>Remote</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Data &amp; BI Consultant</h3>
        <div class="role">Excel · Power Query · Power BI</div>
        <div class="body"><p>I help teams bring data together from several sources, clean it, automate recurring reports and build dashboards people actually use.</p></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">Nov 2022 – Jan 2026</span><small>Engro Corporation<br>Karachi</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Deputy Manager, People Analytics</h3>
        <div class="role">One of Pakistan's largest groups, with businesses in fertilisers, energy, petrochemicals and telecom infrastructure</div>
        <div class="body"><p>I led the modernisation of people analytics reporting, moving the team from manual HR reports to automated, refreshable reporting. Workforce data sat in several SAP HCM instances with no persistent employee ID across them, so I matched records on name, date of birth and national ID in Power Query, building one clean view of well over a million workforce data points ahead of the move to SAP SuccessFactors.</p><p>On that foundation, I built HR reporting first in Excel, then in Power BI and Qlik Sense, covering headcount, talent movements and other workforce metrics. This cut the manual effort behind regular reporting by around 70%, made it possible to report more often, and improved data accuracy. The dashboards were used by the CPO, the CFO and heads of department, and I helped standardise KPI definitions so every report told the same story. I also supported workforce planning with forecasts built on the cleaned data.</p><p>As reporting moved to the cloud, I supported the AWS team with data mapping and validation between SAP SuccessFactors and the new environment. On an HR chatbot proof of concept, I prepared the data, wrote the test questions and checked its answers against the source data.</p><p>I automated work that used to take days, including personalised certificates (PDF and image) and individual emails, each with its own attachments, for 2,500+ employees using Python.</p></div>
        <div class="facts">
          <div class="fact"><b data-n="1" data-suf="M+">1M+</b><span>workforce data points in one view</span></div>
          <div class="fact"><b data-n="70" data-pre="~" data-suf="%">~70%</b><span>less manual effort behind HR reporting</span></div>
          <div class="fact"><b data-n="2500" data-suf="+">2,500+</b><span>personalised certificates and emails</span></div>
        </div><div class="packed"><span class="lab">Tools</span><span class="chip">Power BI</span><span class="chip">Power Query</span><span class="chip">Qlik Sense</span><span class="chip">Python</span><span class="chip">Excel</span><span class="chip">SAP SuccessFactors</span><span class="chip">SAP HCM</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">Jul 2021 – Nov 2022</span><small>SHMA Consulting<br>Karachi · UAE clients</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Assistant Manager</h3>
        <div class="role">Actuarial consulting for insurers in the Middle East and South Asia</div>
        <div class="body"><p>I delivered actuarial and risk analytics for insurers in the UAE, including ADNIC: pricing adequacy models, loss variance analyses and reinsurance reviews that helped clients judge how their portfolios were performing.</p><p>I led a preliminary Workers' Compensation study for the UAE market, testing reinsurance arrangements, pricing and cost-benefit options, backed by research to quantify the expected impact on the P&amp;L. I also prepared regulatory reporting in line with CBUAE requirements.</p><p>I brought actuarial, claims and reinsurance data together with Alteryx and advanced Excel, which cut manual reconciliation and sped up reporting cycles, and designed Qlik dashboards and variance tools that made results easier to follow.</p></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">Jul 2017 – Jun 2021</span><small>SHMA Consulting</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Senior Actuarial Analyst</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>I worked in the team building early IFRS 17 base models in Excel and Power Query, helping insurers prepare for the new standard, and automated key valuation and reporting steps with Excel VBA and Qlik.</p><p>I carried out portfolio reviews for ADNIC covering pricing adequacy, reserving, variance analysis and performance, and supported reinsurance programme reviews, including quota share and excess-of-loss arrangements.</p></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">Jul 2016 – Jun 2017</span><small>SHMA Consulting</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Actuarial Analyst</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>I contributed to reporting, reserving, pricing and capital adequacy work across several insurance portfolios, and automated actuarial workflows with Excel macros and VBA, cutting the time for routine reporting by around 50%.</p><p>I built pricing and reserving models to client requirements, ran scenario-based sensitivity analyses, wrote technical documentation for actuarial audits and supported CBUAE regulatory submissions.</p></div>
        <div class="facts"><div class="fact"><b data-n="50" data-pre="~" data-suf="%">~50%</b><span>less time on routine reporting</span></div></div><div class="packed"><span class="lab">Tools</span><span class="chip">Excel</span><span class="chip">VBA</span><span class="chip">Power Query</span><span class="chip">Alteryx</span><span class="chip">QlikView</span><span class="chip">Qlik Sense</span></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="camp">
      <span class="pin"></span>
      <div class="when"><span class="lab">2009 – 2015</span><small>Bahria University, 2009–2013<br>SZABIST, 2013–2015</small></div>
      <div class="what">
        <h3>Business school</h3>
        <div class="role">BBA Finance · MBA, Business Management and Marketing</div>
        <div class="body"><p>Six years of finance and management, and the first spreadsheet habits.</p></div>
      </div>
